{"name":"Boneyard","hex":"#bb9977","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boneyard","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A graveyard.","In the game of dominoes, the pile of upside-down pieces that have yet to be used."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boneyard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cemetery","blocks":[{"text":"A cemetery, burial ground, gravesite, graveyard, or a green space called a memorial park or memorial garden, is a place where the remains of many dead people are buried or otherwise entombed. The word cemetery implies that the land is specifically designated as a burial ground and originally applied to the Roman catacombs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Kerepesi_temet%C5%91_Budapest.jpg/330px-Kerepesi_temet%C5%91_Budapest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cemetery"},{"title":"Mantra (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Mantra is an American comic book series written by Mike W. Barr, mainly penciled by Terry Dodson and published by Malibu Comics in the mid-1990s, until it was purchased by Marvel Comics. Adam Hughes is credited for the character designs. After the purchase, the title was canceled after 24 issues and revamped in a new version, with a new protagonist."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Mantra_%28Malibu_Comics%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantra_(comics)"},{"title":"Boneyard (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Boneyard is a 2024 American crime thriller film directed by Asif Akbar, produced by Colin Bates, Asif Akbar, and Vincent E. McDaniel, and starring Mel Gibson and 50 Cent. It is based on the West Mesa murders."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/97/Boneyard_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikiped